# 12. The most important distinction

You now have four different levels:

### Level 1 — Symbolic data

```text
cow → moo
```

### Level 2 — IDs

```text
cow → 2
moo → 7
```

These are merely identifiers.

### Level 3 — Embeddings

```text
cow → [0.31, -0.72, 0.44, ...]
```

These are learned numerical representations.

### Level 4 — Transformer computation

The Transformer combines those representations through learned transformations and attention to produce:

```text
probability distribution over possible next tokens
```

Then:

```text
prediction
   ↓
loss
   ↓
gradient
   ↓
weight update
```

And **that is learning**.

