# 11. Contrastive learning

This is another very useful concept for understanding modern AI.

Suppose we give the model:

```text
"dog"
picture of a dog
```

We want their representations to be close.

But:

```text
"dog"
picture of a car
```

should be far apart.

So training says:

```text
similar pair   → pull together
different pair → push apart
```

This produces a learned **representation space**.

You can imagine:

```text
             dog
            /   \
          cat   wolf
           \     /
            animals

                         car
                        /   \
                     truck  bus
```

This is particularly important because neural networks often don't simply learn answers—they learn **representations**.

