# 9. There are actually two different ways constraints can enter

This distinction is particularly interesting.

### A. Constraints during learning

We can influence the model:

```text
training
   ↓
semantic constraint
   ↓
semantic loss
   ↓
gradient
   ↓
updated parameters
```

The model is being **trained to behave better**.

---

### B. Constraints after learning

We can leave the model unchanged:

```text
trained model
     ↓
semantic checker
     ↓
valid? ── YES → accept
     │
     NO
     ↓
reject / repair / ask again
```

This is the guardrail we already implemented.

So:

```text
semantic constraint
       │
       ├── training constraint
       │
       └── runtime constraint
```

And you can actually use **both**.

