# 13. This also explains why formal verification is different from training

Consider:

```text
Training:

"Make violations unlikely."
```

versus:

```text
Formal verification:

"Prove violations impossible under the specified assumptions."
```

Those are radically different claims.

There is also a middle ground:

```text
Training:
    minimize P(violation)

Probabilistic verification:
    prove P(violation) ≤ ε

Formal verification:
    prove violation = impossible
```

This three-level view is extremely useful.

---

# 14. And there is a fourth possibility: verified training

Here's where things get particularly interesting.

Instead of:

```text
train → verify
```

we could potentially have:

