```

This is closely related to the **counterexample-guided** approach we discussed earlier.

The verifier isn't merely saying:

> "You failed."

It can potentially provide a **counterexample**:

```text
Here is an input where your model violates the property.
```

That counterexample can become new training data.

Then:

```text
AI proposes
     ↓
train
     ↓
verify
     ↓
counterexample
     ↓
train again
     ↓
verify again
     ↓
...
```

That is a very interesting bridge between **machine learning and formal methods**.

